# Exclude directories not needed in Docker context
# Frontend build only needs frontend/
# Backend build only needs backend/
scripts/
logs/
docker/
# …except the build-time dependency installer, which backend/Dockerfile COPYs
# into the builder stage. docker/ is otherwise excluded because its contents are
# runtime concerns (compose files, nginx conf, dev-entrypoint.sh — that one is
# bind-mounted, not baked, so it never needed the context).
!docker/uv-sync-extras.sh
# …and the boot-time schema step, which the production image bakes in (the dev
# stack bind-mounts it instead; docker-compose.nova-prod.yaml has no mounts of
# repo files by design).
!scripts/db-migrate.sh
skills/
frontend/.next
frontend/node_modules
backend/.venv
backend/htmlcov
backend/.coverage
# Runtime per-thread data (workspaces, uploads, outputs). Never belongs in the
# build context; contains container-owned files unreadable by the host sender.
backend/.deer-flow
.deer-flow
# Same for the post-rename data dir. Without these the live host's sessions,
# memory and thread files were COPYed into the gateway image by `COPY backend`
# (and root-owned entries made the build fail outright with EACCES).
backend/.nova
.nova
backend/.env
*.md
!README.md
!frontend/README.md
!backend/README.md
